Chapter: BrotliCtx2Test
  cites Compress chapter Brotli

 RFC 7932 context mode 2 (UTF8), read by our decoder.

 GENERATED by build/brotli-ctx2-cases.ps1. Do not edit by hand.

 Our encoder writes context mode ZERO, so nothing our two halves do together
 can exercise mode two. Every stream below was built by an independent
 implementation and its expected byte is what .NET's BrotliStream decodes it
 to, which is the only thing that can judge a reader of a format we do not
 write.

 EACH CASE IS CHOSEN WHERE THE TWO MODES DISAGREE. A stream sets the previous
 two bytes with a stored meta-block, then carries one literal under two trees
 naming A and B, with a context map assigning the tree by one bit of the
 context. The mode-zero context and the mode-two context differ in that bit,
 so a decoder that ignores the context mode field answers the other letter.
 Before 2026-07-19 this reader ignored it and every case here answered wrong.

